<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- App Groups (group.com.echoelmusic) REMOVED 2026-07-19 (ultracode-heal,
	     AUv3 candidate #1). SYMPTOM: EchoelBodyVibe registers (AUM lists it) but
	     fails to INSTANTIATE in EVERY host (AUM "won't open"; our self-probe returns
	     -3000 invalidComponentID) — the host-independent signature of an extension
	     whose process launch iOS DENIES. A common cause is an App-Group entitlement
	     the extension's App ID (com.echoelmusic.app.auv3) is not actually granted in
	     the portal: iOS registers the AudioComponent from Info.plist but refuses to
	     start the appex process → -3000 everywhere, persistent across builds.
	     The AU does NOT need the group to instantiate: BioFeedbackManager's
	     App-Group read (pullSharedVitals, EchoelmusicAudioUnit.swift:367-377)
	     degrades cleanly to "host set the params" when the suite is absent — the
	     plugin still works, it only loses the live main-app->plugin vitals bridge.
	     If a fresh clean-install then OPENS the plugin, this mismatch WAS the gate.
	     To restore the live bridge later: grant App Groups (group.com.echoelmusic)
	     to the com.echoelmusic.app.auv3 App ID in the portal, THEN re-add the key
	     here - do not re-add it before the App ID carries the capability. -->
</dict>
</plist>
